    {
      "id": "12cc0e26058fee1744a152219307b6337375e2cf",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 524331002,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Just for discussion:\nIf the epb_dropcount field is evaluated and dissected (frame.dropcount), I think it could be helpful, if the field \"frame.number\" would also be manipulated, if dropped frames are detected. What do you think? I think, it would be much easier, to detect missing frames, inside big traces...\n\nE.G:\n- frame.number = 1; frame.dropCount = 0;\n- frame.number = 2; frame.dropCount = 0;\n- frame.number = **10**; frame.dropCount = **8**;\n- frame.number = 11; frame.dropCount = 0;\n- and so on...",
          "author": {
            "id": 6726480,
            "username": "christian.krump",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Christian Krump",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c3770f36f6e12374811ecd9d21417250256004bcc89598debdfe977b6c0c981?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/christian.krump"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-03-08T13:15:47.990Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-03-08T13:16:57.046Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 76104889,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 774,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "adc9713fa07e653f65b19f726143a3cf6ca74442",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 524334154,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I don't think it's that simple. `frame.number` is a global incrementing number in the same namespace shared between all interfaces. `frame.dropCount` refers to the number of dropped frames _on that specific interface_.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7506978,
            "username": "dieter-exc",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dieter Dobbelaere",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e773863e2353c853602a4dc97487b94fe58245e3455e511de6c36ddb9668a317?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/dieter-exc"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-03-08T13:20:06.354Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-03-08T13:20:06.354Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 76104889,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 774,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "658eac52d353dae846741e6b573576c403ed1e45",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 524345820,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Maybe it would be an idea, to add an additional dissection field... e.g. frame.ifCount? And this field could visualize the framenumber under consideration of possible dropped frames. If someone needs this feature, a new column with this field could be inserted, or the existing default column could be edited to display the new field.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6726480,
            "username": "christian.krump",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Christian Krump",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
